#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The GeoJSON specification states that polygons are oriented using the Right-"
"Hand Rule, and some clients require this orientation. This can be ensured by"
" using <xref linkend=\"ST_ForcePolygonCCW\"/>. The specification also "
"requires that geometry be in the WGS84 coordinate system (SRID = 4326). If "
"necessary geometry can be projected into WGS84 using <xref "
"linkend=\"ST_Transform\"/>: <code>ST_Transform(geom, 4326 )</code>."
msgstr ""
"GeoJSON-specifikationen anger att polygoner orienteras med högerhandsregeln "
"och vissa klienter kräver denna orientering. Den kan säkerställas med <xref "
"linkend=\"ST_ForcePolygonCCW\"/>. Specifikationen kräver även att geometri "
"är i WGS84-koordinatsystemet (SRID = 4326). Vid behov kan geometri "
"projiceras till WGS84 med <xref linkend=\"ST_Transform\"/>: "
"<code>ST_Transform(geom, 4326 )</code>."

#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function returns a MARC21/XML record with <link "
"xlink:href=\"https://www.loc.gov/marc/bibliographic/bd034.html\">Coded "
"Cartographic Mathematical Data</link> representing the bounding box of a "
"given geometry. The <varname>format</varname> parameter allows to encode the"
" coordinates in subfields "
"<varname>$d</varname>,<varname>$e</varname>,<varname>$f</varname> and "
"<varname>$g</varname> in all formats supported by the MARC21/XML standard. "
"Valid formats are:"
msgstr ""
"Den här funktionen returnerar en MARC21/XML-post med <link "
"xlink:href=\"https://www.loc.gov/marc/bibliographic/bd034.html\">Coded "
"Cartographic Mathematical Data</link> som representerar begränsningsrutan "
"för en given geometri. Parametern <varname>format</varname> gör det möjligt "
"att koda koordinaterna i underfälten <varname>$d</varname>, "
"<varname>$e</varname>, <varname>$f</varname> och <varname>$g</varname> i "
"alla format som stöds av MARC21/XML-standarden. Giltiga format är:"

#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"2: Output coordinates in GeoSpatial GeoCoordinates. This option will throw "
"an error if geometries are not in WGS 84 long lat (srid: 4326). This is "
"currently the only GeoCoordinate type supported. <link "
"xlink:href=\"http://www.web3d.org/documents/specifications/19775-1/V3.2/Part01/components/geodata.html#Specifyingaspatialreference\">Refer"
" to X3D specs specifying a spatial reference system.</link>. Default output "
"will be <code>GeoCoordinate geoSystem='\"GD\" \"WE\" "
"\"longitude_first\"'</code>. If you prefer the X3D default of "
"<code>GeoCoordinate geoSystem='\"GD\" \"WE\" \"latitude_first\"'</code> use "
"<code>(2 + 1)</code> = <code>3</code>"
msgstr ""
"2: Matar ut koordinater i GeoSpatial GeoCoordinates. Det här alternativet "
"utlöser ett fel om geometrierna inte är i WGS 84 long lat (srid: 4326). "
"Detta är för närvarande den enda GeoCoordinate-typen som stöds. <link "
"xlink:href=\"http://www.web3d.org/documents/specifications/19775-1/V3.2/Part01/components/geodata.html#Specifyingaspatialreference\">Refer"
" to X3D specs specifying a spatial reference system.</link>. Standardutdata "
"blir <code>GeoCoordinate geoSystem='\"GD\" \"WE\" "
"\"longitude_first\"'</code>. Om du föredrar X3D-standarden "
"<code>GeoCoordinate geoSystem='\"GD\" \"WE\" \"latitude_first\"'</code> "
"använder du <code>(2 + 1)</code> = <code>3</code>"

#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns a geometry representing the part of geometry A that does not "
"intersect geometry B. This is equivalent to <code>A - "
"ST_Intersection(A,B)</code>. If A is completely contained in B then an empty"
" atomic geometry of appropriate type is returned."
msgstr ""
"Returnerar en geometri som representerar den del av geometri A som inte skär"
" geometri B. Detta motsvarar <code>A - ST_Intersection(A,B)</code>. Om A är "
"helt innesluten i B returneras en tom atomgeometri av lämplig typ."

#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returns a geometry representing the portions of geometries A and B that do "
"not intersect. This is equivalent to <code>ST_Union(A,B) - "
"ST_Intersection(A,B)</code>. It is called a symmetric difference because "
"<code>ST_SymDifference(A,B) = ST_SymDifference(B,A)</code>."
msgstr ""
"Returnerar en geometri som representerar de delar av geometrierna A och B "
"som inte skär varandra. Detta motsvarar <code>ST_Union(A,B) - "
"ST_Intersection(A,B)</code>. Det kallas en symmetrisk differens eftersom "
"<code>ST_SymDifference(A,B) = ST_SymDifference(B,A)</code>."

#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another use of this function is to node and dissolve a collection of "
"linestrings which cross or overlap to make them <link "
"linkend=\"Simple_Geometry\">simple</link>. (<xref linkend=\"ST_Node\"/> also"
" does this, but it does not provide the <code>gridSize</code> option.)"
msgstr ""
"En annan användning av funktionen är att nodera och lösa upp en samling "
"linjesträngar som korsar eller överlappar varandra för att göra dem <link "
"linkend=\"Simple_Geometry\">simple</link>. (<xref linkend=\"ST_Node\"/> gör "
"också detta, men tillhandahåller inte alternativet <code>gridSize</code>.)"
